  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.24:\n\t\t- Fixed: ToDateTimeUtc(long)/ToDateTimeUtcFromMs(long) now clamp to DateTime.MinValue/DateTime.MaxValue\n\t\t  instead of throwing ArgumentOutOfRangeException when the epoch value is out of DateTime's representable\n\t\t  range. Some LogicMonitor SDTs return a corrupted start/end date/time that previously crashed any consumer\n\t\t  reading ScheduledDownTime/HistoricScheduledDownTime.StartDateTimeUtc/EndDateTimeUtc, Alert.LastUpdatedOnUtc,\n\t\t  or ResourceDataSourceInstanceConfig.PollUtc.\n\t\t- Removed unused ToDateTimeFromMsUtc and ToSecondLevel from DateTimeExtensions (dead code, no callers).",
